{"availability":"available","full":"retracn/youtube-transcript-cloud-js","name":"youtube-transcript-cloud-js","description":"Drop-in replacement for the youtube-transcript npm package that works in production (Vercel, AWS Lambda, Render): same API and errors, no blocked requests.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-06T00:44:39Z","updated":"2026-10-06T00:44:44Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://retracn.github.io/automationnation-actors/guides/youtube-transcript-npm-not-working-in-production/","topics":["apify","captions","nextjs","nodejs","npm","serverless","transcript","vercel","youtube","youtube-transcript"],"demo":"https://retracn.github.io/automationnation-actors/guides/youtube-transcript-npm-not-working-in-production/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:20:24.982Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:20:24.982Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:20:24.982Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T15:46:03.326Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T18:20:24.982Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The youtube-transcript npm package fetches captions straight from YouTube, from wherever your code runs. That works on your laptop. But YouTube distrusts cloud IPs (Vercel, AWS Lambda, Render, Railway, Fly, Google Cloud), so in production it often throws YoutubeTranscriptDisabledError for videos that do have captions, or returns nothing. See its issues \"Doesn't work in production\" and \"works locally but throws YoutubeTranscriptDisabledError on Render\".","youtube-transcript-cloud keeps the same API, output and error classes, so your code doesn't change. Each request runs on a hosted transcript API that deals with YouTube's blocks, so it behaves the same everywhere."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/retracn/youtube-transcript-cloud-js/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fa7c356f27c32b374